jules_sales: Heads-up — Meridian Ledger (enterprise payments) is evaluating a swap from their current provider. They need EU data residency, strict key controls, and a near-drop-in API so product teams don't rewrite clients. Can we scope a short presales POC?
rada_se: Which exact API surface are they using today? Are they heavy on streaming updates and function-style tool calls or mostly single-turn completions + embeddings?
sam_infra: Infra asks: private peering preferred, require static egress IPs and mTLS client certs for all connections. If they insist on HSM-backed keys + rotation logs, Private/Dedicated is our primary offer. Hosted might work if they accept a managed KMS.
leah_sec: Request their security questionnaire (SSQ/SIG). Also check regulatory controls for EU data residency and breach notification windows. We should surface SOC2/ISO docs and encryption-at-rest details.
toni_integration: From past migrations, the tricky diffs are (1) stop-sequence vs token-based truncation, (2) function-call payload shape, (3) streaming chunk framing and event names. We can deliver a lightweight compatibility layer that translates their HTTP contract to our shape and applies deterministic postprocessing.
rada_se: Pricing: they currently charge per-event (their "api_call_unit"). They want revenue-neutral billing mapping. We'll need a representative traffic capture (24-72h) to compute average tokens per call and propose per-call equivalence.
jules_sales: I'll ask Meridian for 72h logs and a sample SLA/contract language by EOD. Also confirm monthly spend.
sam_infra: SLA note: 99.95 requires reserved capacity + cross-region DR runbook. Hosted standard is 99.9, but we can propose a dedicated pool in eu-west with standby capacity. There's a cost delta; I'll provide an uplift estimate.
leah_sec: Compliance gap: they require quarterly pen-tests and a contractual window for findings. Also request for legal: DPA language, subprocessor list, and penetration testing scope. @legalbot can you prepare a template?
legalbot: Preparing DPA + pen-test clause template. Will forward redlines.
toni_integration: Quick shim sketch (JS):
```
// translate incoming vendor body -> Redwood API
const mappedReq = {
  prompt: vendor.body.prompt_text,
  max_tokens: vendor.body.limit || 512,
  stop: normalizeStops(vendor.body.stop_sequences)
};
// stream mapping: vendor expects 'on_delta' events with {chunk, done}
redwood.stream(mappedReq, (delta) => {
  const event = { chunk: delta.text, done: delta.done }
  vendorCallback(event)
});
```
toni_integration: Also recommend post-processing for function-calls: reserialize args to their expected schema and preserve call ordering by enforcing single-call-first semantics.
rada_se: For behavioral parity testing let's run a 500-sample harness (200 smoke + 300 strain cases). Compare top-3 outputs, token usage, and function-call equivalence. If deltas >7% for critical flows, propose model variant changes or additional prompt engineering.
jules_sales: Actions: (1) I'll collect 72h logs + spend + their SSQ; (2) schedule 45m tech deep-dive Tue 11am CET with @toni_integration and @leah_sec; (3) Toni to produce a shim POC and run the 200-smoke by Friday; (4) Sam to provide static egress options and cost delta.
sam_infra: Will list peering options, NAT partners, and rough reserved capacity uplift today.
leah_sec: I'll start drafting SSQ answers and note BYOK/HSM gaps.
toni_integration: Will spin up a simple shim repo and push initial scripts to git.redwood/presales/meridian-swap.
opsbot: Presales repo created: git.redwood/presales/meridian-swap (bootstrap + test harness).
jules_sales: Thanks all 44d Meridian timeline is tight (2-3 weeks). I'll keep them informed and share logs when available.
